(890169, 101923, 2764, '<td valign="top">Nice camera work, would have been good for the deep DOF challenge as well.  i like the contrast of the bark to the grass.  however neither the tree trunks nor the scene they frame is ver interesting.  I bet that tree in the center is lovely, if you could just cut down al the surrounding foliage the phot would be much stronger.</td>', 'Nice camera work, would have been good for the deep DOF challenge as well.  i like the contrast of the bark to the grass.  however neither the tree trunks nor the scene they frame is ver interesting.  I bet that tree in the center is lovely, if you could just cut down al the surrounding foliage the phot would be much stronger.', '2004-09-02 19:08:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(890170, 101675, 6999, '<td valign="top">Well this just has to be JJ. Very nice to see that more recent stuff, those detached candid studies, being combined with the architectural work we all know you so well for. I like the indignificance of this child against the loom of the archways, and the parallel disinterst of the child in his surroundings. Great balance. I suppose I should add that if this isn''t JJ, then it''s the best impression of someone''s style I''ve ever seen.</td>', 'Well this just has to be JJ. Very nice to see that more recent stuff, those detached candid studies, being combined with the architectural work we all know you so well for. I like the indignificance of this child against the loom of the archways, and the parallel disinterst of the child in his surroundings. Great balance. I suppose I should add that if this isn''t JJ, then it''s the best impression of someone''s style I''ve ever seen.', '2004-09-02 19:10:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(890172, 100397, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good shot. The stone-work generally seems to lack a little punch - I would personally have pushed it a little harder with curves or something, just to bring out the contrast there more. That said, that quality does allow the compositional thing with the tree to come out well. Can''t quite see it on the front page, but I couldn''t say why it doesn''t deserve to be there. very good, actually. 9</td>', 'Good shot. The stone-work generally seems to lack a little punch - I would personally have pushed it a little harder with curves or something, just to bring out the contrast there more. That said, that quality does allow the compositional thing with the tree to come out well. Can''t quite see it on the front page, but I couldn''t say why it doesn''t deserve to be there. very good, actually. 9', '2004-09-02 19:14:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(890174, 101346, 2764, '<td valign="top">eww - you''re going to lose points for that border - i''ll try to ignore it  The clse up leaves have wonderfil shapes and make an effectve border - I like that half the frame is the big leaves and half is the smaller further away leaves.</td>', 'eww - you''re going to lose points for that border - i''ll try to ignore it  The clse up leaves have wonderfil shapes and make an effectve border - I like that half the frame is the big leaves and half is the smaller further away leaves.', '2004-09-02 19:16:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(890175, 100797, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''d have liked for there to be more flowers - this way they''re perhaps more of an occasional intrusion than a framing device. I also wonder whether you might not have placed that fountain slightly differently within that frame of flowers - there''s rather a lot of open water, and it doesn''t have the interest to hold the eye, for me. Approaching a good shot though.</td>', 'I''d have liked for there to be more flowers - this way they''re perhaps more of an occasional intrusion than a framing device. I also wonder whether you might not have placed that fountain slightly differently within that frame of flowers - there''s rather a lot of open water, and it doesn''t have the interest to hold the eye, for me. Approaching a good shot though.', '2004-09-02 19:16:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(890177, 101602, 6999, '<td valign="top">I try to be open-minded with challenge interpretations, but this one I fear I really cannot see. A kind of interesting photograph though, for all that - just a touch too simply odd for my taste. 4</td>', 'I try to be open-minded with challenge interpretations, but this one I fear I really cannot see. A kind of interesting photograph though, for all that - just a touch too simply odd for my taste. 4', '2004-09-02 19:18:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(890180, 101952, 6999, '<td valign="top">Fun. That fractional over-exposure (even for the technique) on the paper leaves some annoying artefacts around the tears, and that light is not particularly effective on the face behind either. Something softer perhaps? Although i appreciate that that would remve the striking starkness, and thus some of the angry quality, of those paper shadows. 7</td>', 'Fun. That fractional over-exposure (even for the technique) on the paper leaves some annoying artefacts around the tears, and that light is not particularly effective on the face behind either. Something softer perhaps? Although i appreciate that that would remve the striking starkness, and thus some of the angry quality, of those paper shadows. 7', '2004-09-02 19:21:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(890181, 101700, 6999, '<td valign="top">Big-time fill flash? Effectively done, too - and has allowed those colours in the underside of the leaves through nicely. Good light control and blalnce overall, perhaps let down a touch by that branch intruding so heavily in frame? An unobscured view of the house would make less of a feature of the branches and more of a frame, but these are minor points. Atouch too much on the big brght sunny day side for my taste, but a very well executed shot nevertheless.</td>', 'Big-time fill flash? Effectively done, too - and has allowed those colours in the underside of the leaves through nicely. Good light control and blalnce overall, perhaps let down a touch by that branch intruding so heavily in frame? An unobscured view of the house would make less of a feature of the branches and more of a frame, but these are minor points. Atouch too much on the big brght sunny day side for my taste, but a very well executed shot nevertheless.', '2004-09-02 19:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(890183, 101680, 6999, '<td valign="top">Whilst I like this, i cannot quite let it stand on the challenge front. Would lke to have felt less like I was hidden from the bug, too - but the colour rendition is great.</td>', 'Whilst I like this, i cannot quite let it stand on the challenge front. Would lke to have felt less like I was hidden from the bug, too - but the colour rendition is great.', '2004-09-02 19:26:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(890185, 100514, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good landscape work indeed. Despite your title, it doesn''t meet the challenge though, does it? Control of light is very well done -  almost has the feeling of being a composite shot - those clouds and the snow surely ought to be way brighter than the trees? Excellently done on that side of things.</td>', 'Good landscape work indeed. Despite your title, it doesn''t meet the challenge though, does it? Control of light is very well done -  almost has the feeling of being a composite shot - those clouds and the snow surely ought to be way brighter than the trees? Excellently done on that side of things.', '2004-09-02 19:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(890190, 101501, 6999, '<td valign="top">This is spookily familiar - I''ve either been there or seen it in a book. It wouldn''t be one of the Landmark Trust proerties in the Uk would it? I do like the organisation of those strong graphical elements within this frame, and the tonality you''ve achieved here. The only thing I would like more of would be texture in that stone - it all seems a touch flat. Minor point, but significant. 8</td>', 'This is spookily familiar - I''ve either been there or seen it in a book. It wouldn''t be one of the Landmark Trust proerties in the Uk would it? I do like the organisation of those strong graphical elements within this frame, and the tonality you''ve achieved here. The only thing I would like more of would be texture in that stone - it all seems a touch flat. Minor point, but significant. 8', '2004-09-02 19:37:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(890194, 101520, 6999, '<td valign="top">Do i sense the hand of the perilous Neatimage here? it has something of that slightly exaggerated sharpening and loss of detail inother areas that can come from that. That said - wonderful moment, wonderful light, great composition - with the proviso that it feels a touch too centrally balanced: I think framing this with the most important subjects more thoroughly ditricuted around frame would give it a greater sense of stability: for instance, nice as the light in the clouds is, lsoing a little of it would place that largest rock more strongly, and i think the whole image would come together that bit more strongly - and trying it by scrolling to obscure just below that topmost branch seems to back that up. Have you tried that? Otherwise, a very fine shot indeed. 7</td>', 'Do i sense the hand of the perilous Neatimage here? it has something of that slightly exaggerated sharpening and loss of detail inother areas that can come from that. That said - wonderful moment, wonderful light, great composition - with the proviso that it feels a touch too centrally balanced: I think framing this with the most important subjects more thoroughly ditricuted around frame would give it a greater sense of stability: for instance, nice as the light in the clouds is, lsoing a little of it would place that largest rock more strongly, and i think the whole image would come together that bit more strongly - and trying it by scrolling to obscure just below that topmost branch seems to back that up. Have you tried that? Otherwise, a very fine shot indeed. 7', '2004-09-02 19:41:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(890198, 101315, 6999, '<td valign="top">Has the oddest quality of being a scan - it just doesn''t feel like a digital photograph. Or maybe I''m seeing some other quality.</td>', 'Has the oddest quality of being a scan - it just doesn''t feel like a digital photograph. Or maybe I''m seeing some other quality.', '2004-09-02 19:48:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(890204, 101038, 24642, '<td valign="top">I did refresh my screen twice but still the picture is damaged.</td>', 'I did refresh my screen twice but still the picture is damaged.', '2004-09-02 19:53:51.000000', NULL, 1),
