(890474, 101952, 22671, '<td valign="top">The contrast between the seriousness of the person''s face and the light-heartedness of the picture is delightful.  The lighting on the ripped areas is a bit too strong for me.  It makes the shreds seem to glow against their shadows and it takes some attention away from the main subject, the face.  Still a great pic.</td>', 'The contrast between the seriousness of the person''s face and the light-heartedness of the picture is delightful.  The lighting on the ripped areas is a bit too strong for me.  It makes the shreds seem to glow against their shadows and it takes some attention away from the main subject, the face.  Still a great pic.', '2004-09-03 00:16:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(890476, 101007, 24704, '<td valign="top">very relaxing   good framing</td>', 'very relaxing   good framing', '2004-09-03 00:17:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(890478, 101768, 22671, '<td valign="top">I love the soft, dreamlike quality of the picture, and the use of just a few basic familiar colors to give this picture a very nostalgic mood.  Great photo!</td>', 'I love the soft, dreamlike quality of the picture, and the use of just a few basic familiar colors to give this picture a very nostalgic mood.  Great photo!', '2004-09-03 00:18:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(890481, 101680, 22671, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors.  Beautiful capture.  Did you leave the bug slightly out of focus to keep it more consistent with the rest of the picture?</td>', 'Beautiful colors.  Beautiful capture.  Did you leave the bug slightly out of focus to keep it more consistent with the rest of the picture?', '2004-09-03 00:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(890482, 101826, 24704, '<td valign="top">great</td>', 'great', '2004-09-03 00:23:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(890487, 100550, 22671, '<td valign="top">I''d love to see what the color version looks like.  I feel like the type of subject (flora) and the complex detail of the picture would lend itself to be better represented in color.  In B&amp;W, the stuff on the upper right coner of the door frame has too much going on for my eyes and it just becomes a big complicated blob of distraction without colors to help the brain figure out what''s what.</td>', 'I''d love to see what the color version looks like.  I feel like the type of subject (flora) and the complex detail of the picture would lend itself to be better represented in color.  In B&W, the stuff on the upper right coner of the door frame has too much going on for my eyes and it just becomes a big complicated blob of distraction without colors to help the brain figure out what''s what.', '2004-09-03 00:29:29.000000', NULL, 1),
