(890761, 100661, 6999, '<td valign="top">The compositional elements of this shot are really quite interesting - so it''s perhaps interesting to think about why it doesn''t work, at least for me, which it certainly doesn''t. Your sky here is pretty flat and monotonous, which perhaps doesn''t help - though one would think that just pushed the interest to the bridge and railway. The actual organisation of elements across the frame is a touch weak - the vanishing point of the railway, and indeed the tracks themselves are relegated to a very small corner of the image, making them lose some impact. There''s a lack of detail here too - that fine resolution that would show the textures of the bridge, and the vegetation beside the tracks. A scene that has great potential, I think - but in the end let down by composition (the placement of the rails relative to the bridge) and very simply poor overly-general light. Nothing I think you could have done about the weather I know, but nevertheless that is what lets it down.</td>', 'The compositional elements of this shot are really quite interesting - so it''s perhaps interesting to think about why it doesn''t work, at least for me, which it certainly doesn''t. Your sky here is pretty flat and monotonous, which perhaps doesn''t help - though one would think that just pushed the interest to the bridge and railway. The actual organisation of elements across the frame is a touch weak - the vanishing point of the railway, and indeed the tracks themselves are relegated to a very small corner of the image, making them lose some impact. There''s a lack of detail here too - that fine resolution that would show the textures of the bridge, and the vegetation beside the tracks. A scene that has great potential, I think - but in the end let down by composition (the placement of the rails relative to the bridge) and very simply poor overly-general light. Nothing I think you could have done about the weather I know, but nevertheless that is what lets it down.', '2004-09-03 05:52:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(890762, 101927, 18757, '<td valign="top">did you shot it behind the glass?? I like the colors and composition much...</td>', 'did you shot it behind the glass?? I like the colors and composition much...', '2004-09-03 05:56:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(890763, 100719, 6999, '<td valign="top">Lovely, fascinating, involving composition. A touch too far on the sharpening perhaps? That always shows particularly strongly on diagonal lines, of course - especially in that image right little section between the frosted glass areas of the first doors. Really like the subsidiary, image-within-image work here, the difficulty of finding a route through the chaos of reflections to the ''real'' - a neat critique of the corporate world, in its way.</td>', 'Lovely, fascinating, involving composition. A touch too far on the sharpening perhaps? That always shows particularly strongly on diagonal lines, of course - especially in that image right little section between the frosted glass areas of the first doors. Really like the subsidiary, image-within-image work here, the difficulty of finding a route through the chaos of reflections to the ''real'' - a neat critique of the corporate world, in its way.', '2004-09-03 05:58:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(890764, 101348, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good tonality, especially the grass colours.</td>', 'Good tonality, especially the grass colours.', '2004-09-03 06:00:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(890766, 101933, 6999, '<td valign="top">Like the toning very much, like the feel you''ve generated in the grass, and those hanging strings from the tree (they have a name, those things, though I can''t recall it right now). Somehow, though, the shot overall doesn''t do enough for me. It might be the sher arbitrariness of those two stones: it somehow lacks real mystery. Struggling to explain - but something isn''t cutting it for me. 7</td>', 'Like the toning very much, like the feel you''ve generated in the grass, and those hanging strings from the tree (they have a name, those things, though I can''t recall it right now). Somehow, though, the shot overall doesn''t do enough for me. It might be the sher arbitrariness of those two stones: it somehow lacks real mystery. Struggling to explain - but something isn''t cutting it for me. 7', '2004-09-03 06:06:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(890767, 101574, 12316, '<td valign="top">The light is on your hand instead on the dog ... and the ideea of framing something with your hands ... sorry but not so good ...</td>', 'The light is on your hand instead on the dog ... and the ideea of framing something with your hands ... sorry but not so good ...', '2004-09-03 06:06:56.000000', NULL, 1),
