(988095, 101693, 25665, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Momo:</b></div><hr/><i> Very cool picture.  The only thing I see that might be improved is the light shining on the face seems too strong.  It washes out the color of the skin.  Maybe use a tinted light?  I would have preferred some deeper colored eyes for this picture like a rich blue or green.  Most of the picture is gray aluminum, so for the subject to really stand out, you''d want a more pure color than the greyish eyes and almost white skin.... unless you were going for consistency with the color of the frame.  I personally think that strong contrast between the frame and the subject would work better here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks a lot. Very useful comment. Yet there is an explanation for the washout color of the skin ... It was round 6AM and there was a lot of redness around the retina - don''t ask me why :). So I did some levels. A little too much it seems. <br/>I would have used some blue eyes too, but mine are green - grayish and the only ones I could find that morning :D.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 06:27:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Momo: Very cool picture.  The only thing I see that might be improved is the light shining on the face seems too strong.  It washes out the color of the skin.  Maybe use a tinted light?  I would have preferred some deeper colored eyes for this picture like a rich blue or green.  Most of the picture is gray aluminum, so for the subject to really stand out, you''d want a more pure color than the greyish eyes and almost white skin.... unless you were going for consistency with the color of the frame.  I personally think that strong contrast between the frame and the subject would work better here.   Thanks a lot. Very useful comment. Yet there is an explanation for the washout color of the skin ... It was round 6AM and there was a lot of redness around the retina - don''t ask me why :). So I did some levels. A little too much it seems. I would have used some blue eyes too, but mine are green - grayish and the only ones I could find that morning :D.', '2004-11-03 06:26:57.000000', '2004-11-03 06:27:53.000000', 0),
(988112, 101693, 25665, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ximending:</b></div><hr/><i> Title? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, the picture has a title. Try George Orwell''s 1984. Or at least this:<br/><a href="//www.online-literature.com/orwell/1984/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.online-literature.com/orwell/1984/</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 06:42:39.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ximending: Title?  Yes, the picture has a title. Try George Orwell''s 1984. Or at least this://www.online-literature.com/orwell/1984/', '2004-11-03 06:41:48.000000', '2004-11-03 06:42:39.000000', 0),
(988177, 101693, 25665, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by just-married:</b></div><hr/><i> Love the concept.  Not sure the best thing to see is an eye though.  Or if you''re married to the big brother idea, perhaps something other than a can.  I just don''t draw much connection between "can" and "big brother theory".  6 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Imagine you can''t hide even in a beer can from Big Brother''s eye. <br/>Can u? <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 07:52:16.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by just-married: Love the concept.  Not sure the best thing to see is an eye though.  Or if you''re married to the big brother idea, perhaps something other than a can.  I just don''t draw much connection between "can" and "big brother theory".  6  Imagine you can''t hide even in a beer can from Big Brother''s eye. Can u? ', '2004-11-03 07:49:17.000000', '2004-11-03 07:52:16.000000', 0),
